The provided `SafeMaybeObserver` is a thin delegating wrapper whose primary purpose is safety (exception handling) rather than computational work. Its methods simply forward calls to another `MaybeObserver` with minimal logic, and performance characteristics are dominated by the downstream observer and the surrounding RxJava infrastructure. Consequently, a dedicated JMH benchmark for this class would not yield meaningful insights; performance testing should target higher‑level reactive pipelines instead.